<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Congress of People's Deputies of Russia</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1990–1993</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Congress of People's Deputies of the RSFSR</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Congress of People's Deputies of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a> was the highest legislative body of the Russian SFSR and then the Russian Federation from 1990 to 1993. Elected in March 1990 in the republic's first competitive elections, it chose <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/boris-yeltsin">Boris Yeltsin</a> as chairman of its Supreme Soviet and adopted the Declaration of State <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sovereignty">Sovereignty</a> on 12 June 1990. Yeltsin's decree dissolving it in September 1993 led to a violent constitutional crisis.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/congress-of-peoples-deputies-of-russia.jpg" alt="Congress of People's Deputies of Russia" width="320" height="355" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Emblem of the Russian SFSR.svg: Pianist derivative work: FM-K (talk) · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Coat_of_arms_of_the_Russian_Federation_(1992-1993).svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
